From e052b81c23e5fb5a5009ea0fe1ab7ce9bdcd905d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:13:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] demux: gme: keep the track index in range at end of
 playback

The track index is advanced before it is tested, so when the last track
ends it is left equal to the track count and stays there while the demux
object remains open. Every control that indexes titlev[] guards against
exactly that and bails out, so DEMUX_SET_POSITION and DEMUX_GET_LENGTH
fail from then on: the file cannot be sought back to the start to be
repeated, and dragging the seek bar after playback has ended does
nothing. Single track files are affected too, the index simply becomes 1.

Test before advancing, so the index stays on the last track.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/gme.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/gme.c b/modules/demux/gme.c
index 47169d7adf..d9de5f4354 100644
--- a/modules/demux/gme.c
+++ b/modules/demux/gme.c
@@ -227,9 +227,15 @@ static int Demux (demux_t *demux)
     if (gme_track_ended (sys->emu))
     {
         msg_Dbg (demux, "track %u ended", sys->track_id);
-        if (++sys->track_id >= (unsigned)gme_track_count (sys->emu))
+        /* Test before advancing: running the index past the last track
+         * leaves it out of range for good, and every control that indexes
+         * titlev[] bails on that, so seeking and the length are lost once
+         * playback has ended. */
+        if (sys->track_id + 1 >= (unsigned)gme_track_count (sys->emu))
             return VLC_DEMUXER_EOF;
 
+        sys->track_id++;
+
         sys->title_changed = true;
         gme_start_track (sys->emu, sys->track_id);
     }
